# LF everywhere, enforced by git as well as by the normaliser.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf converts to CRLF on checkout on Windows, the normaliser
# converts back to LF, and `fabctl normalise --check` reports every file dirty forever.
# Two tools disagreeing about line endings is a loop nobody wins, so git is told to stay
# out of it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary

# The ledger is append-only and hash-chained. Any transformation on checkout would break
# the chain, so it is treated as opaque bytes.
ledger/**/*.jsonl -text
